tps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122327#issuecomment-5273761251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122327","id":5273761251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOlc14w","user":{"login":"fqqf","id":77983090,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTgzMDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77983090?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf","html_url":"https://github.com/fqqf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-12T22:58:59Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T22:58:59Z","body":"> You are either updating the path too frequently and / or have a too large polygon layout and scale so you are running into precision issues that make your agent \"edge-dance\".\n> \n> See frequent agent problems https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/navigation/navigation_using_navigationagents.html#pathfollowing-common-problems\n\nPolygon is big. So do i have to make a bunch of small ones instead to fix this? Is there some built in solution for this?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5273761251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5275195080","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122327#issuecomment-5275195080","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122327","id":5275195080,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOm0WyA","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-13T02:23:42Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T02:23:42Z","body":"You could slice your level layout into multiple regions chunks.\nThat would break up very long edges. Also helps with navmesh rebaking performance.\n\nSee demo [navigation_mesh_chunks](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/2d/navigation_mesh_chunks) and doc [navigation-mesh-chunks-for-large-worlds](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/navigation/navigation_using_navigationmeshes.html#baking-navigation-mesh-chunks-for-large-worlds) documentation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5275195080/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5282596201","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122327#issuecomment-5282596201","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122327","id":5282596201,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOt4FaQ","user":{"login":"fqqf","id":77983090,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTgzMDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77983090?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf","html_url":"https://github.com/fqqf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fqqf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-13T15:38:35Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T15:38:35Z","body":"Alright, thanks for the links. the problem was I was using too big of a region, and was overlapping it with other region of other layer.\n\n> You could slice your level layout into multiple regions chunks. That would break up very long edges. Also helps with navmesh rebaking performance.\n> \n> See demo [navigation_mesh_chunks](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/2d/navigation_mesh_chunks) and doc [navigation-mesh-chunks-for-large-worlds](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/navigation/navigation_using_navigationmeshes.html#baking-navigation-mesh-chunks-for-large-worlds) documentation.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5282596201/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]